<p>Life has been a little busy. Here's a post shouting out things I've been making lately. The last few weeks have been the end of many projects: very high-output and fun. Some are secret and will come out soon, but here are a few already out in the world.</p>

<h2>Printmaking</h2>
<p>I've been printmaking for 2+ years now, but this is the first print I was proud of in a long time. I turned out this one recently, of a scene in autumn in my college, and I think it came out just how I wanted it. My favourite printmaker, David Weller, who is also a gardener in Oxford and started learning lino around the same time as me, sent me a really kind email about it, which made my entire week honestly. I'm looking forward to catching up with him about printmaking and giving him a copy.</p>

