<h2>Magazine</h2>

<p><a href="https://follymagazine.org" target="_blank">Folly Magazine</a> is a magazine started by my friends, mostly Mertonians. I work on design—this time doing parts of the lay-in, which was new and exciting (I love thinking about type). We designed it to look like a funky small book. I got my art teacher Sarah to write a piece about her approach to drawing through a story about an octopus in Hawaii. She's very dear to me. We launched a week ago. Nearly sold out now—who said Oxford magazines are debt machines? I don't know if we'll do another issue since many of us are graduating. But I've enjoyed this enough that I'll likely start another magazine after graduation. I love print media. I've started appreciating writing more. And I love events. Perfect combination. Volume 2 pieces will be on the website soon.</p>

