<h2>Radio</h2>
<p>Faye and I started a radio <a href="https://www.mixcloud.com/oxideradio_live/pocket-melody-1-29-january-2026/" target="_blank">show</a> with <a href="https://www.oxideradio.live/" target="_blank">Oxide Radio</a> in Oxford. Brazilian percussionists Rosa Rhafa and Nelton Essi visited our college for workshops and concerts—we played alongside them and got extremely inspired. We've been experiencing music differently ever since, living it and breathing it. Radio shows like NTS have been helping us discover new music. Why not make one to share ours? It's called pocket melody—we share songs that are dear to us, that you should keep in your pocket. Unfortunately, it was a deep research deadline when this episode was recorded, so I was on my laptop for most of it, far from the mic, so I sound a bit silly. Hopefully next time I'll learn how to speak into the mic. Stay tuned for future shows.</p>

